    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37432" root="لب" body-key="l">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَبِيبٌ</span></b>  (tropical:)  <i>A person of understanding,</i> or <i>intelligence:</i> pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَلِبَّاءُ</span>. (S, K.) No other broken pl.
is formed from it. (Sb.) Fem. with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ة</span>. (TA.)
See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لُبٌّ</span>, and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَلْبُوبٌ</span>. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  In the following verse
of El-Mudarrib Ibn-Kaab,
“<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَقُلْتُ لَهَا فِيئِى إِلَيْكِ فَإِنَّنِى</span><br />
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَرَامٌ وَإِنِّى بَعْدَ ذَاكِ لَبِيبُ</span><br />
”
by <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بعد ذاك</span> is meant <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مع ذاك</span>; and by <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لبيب</span>,
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُقِيم</span>, (remaining, or staying,) or, accord. to some,
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُلَبٍّ</span>, from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">التَّلْبِيَة</span>: see art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لبى</span>. (S.)

